{"title":"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a geometric progression with n terms have first term one, common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are not zero. The sum of the geometric progression formed by replacing each term of the original progression by its reciprocal is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb89ad2d050876a13bb543f74847f18df286203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{s}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{r^ns}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{s}{r^{n-1}}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{r^n}{s}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{r^{n-1}}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"448\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of a geometric series with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms, initial term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45a551f4331bce5e627f9dd558f542106c75184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a(1-r^n)}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108a0f4ccdccd2e530620186f567c1b71eb67824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\frac{(1-r^n)}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"102\" height=\"42\" />. Our initial sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de364725e05e3d12b8e8ab2f35af544b3df233ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, r, r^2, \\dots, r^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, and replacing each terms with its reciprocal gives us the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9722bdf04f6255c77b2ba9df67875b81ab2b87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, \\frac{1}{r}, \\frac{1}{r^2}, \\dots, \\frac{1}{r^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"119\" height=\"37\" />. The sum is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4316c63ad455fd48e12faeb961c03134d007b7a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-(\\frac{1}{r^n})}{1-\\frac{1}{r}}=\\frac{\\frac{(1-r^n)}{r^n}}{\\frac{1-r}{r}}=\\frac{s}{r^{n-1}}\\Rightarrow \\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"261\" height=\"49\" />.~MathJams\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME\" title=\"1976 AHSME\">1976 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1976 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME\" title=\"1977 AHSME\">1977 AHSME</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Proble